    "description": "Weighing indicator, as part of a non-automatic weighing instrument, designated the D1050. Designed to be used as part of a Class III or IIII non-automatic weighing instrument; operates as single-interval, multi-interval or multi-range; self-indicating; mains or DC powered. Stainless steel and ABS enclosure, 10.4\" graphic LCD display, up to 4 A/D conversion modules, main board with processor. Peripheral devices: initial zero setting, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, automatic zero setting (negative load indications for more than 5 s), semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, zero indicator, preset tare, data storage device, up to 4 load receptors with summation, weighbridge modes (AdR, RcD, RpD)."
